    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters 2026-06-14 with a high-ceiling offensive setup, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (79.46) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), who represent our strongest daily plays. **Corbin Carroll** thrives against the favorable xERA of Abbott, utilizing his elite speed in a plus-matchup to anchor the scoring floor. Meanwhile, **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a highly exploitable matchup against Sugano; his proximity to the heart of the order provides the necessary RBI leverage to push his efficiency score near the 80-threshold. **Jose Caballero** remains a sneaky, high-upside start (75.83) as the dynamic platoon advantage against Corbin yields a significant boost that outweighs his middle-order placement.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was excluding **Max Muncy** (57.67) from the primary rotation, as he sat just outside the elite tier. Despite a favorable xERA from Sugano, **Max Muncy** was suppressed by a lower lineup position and a neutral platoon outcome, making him a marginal play compared to the higher-leveraged opportunities provided by **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**. **Austin Riley** (53.34) also borders on marginal, with his value slightly dragged down by a tougher matchup against Peralta and the defensive efficiency of the opposing battery, though he remains in the UTIL slot due to the lack of viable alternatives on the bench. \n\nRisks for today center on the platoon-heavy nature of our lineup. **Dalton Rushing** (47.18) and **Alex Freeland** (51.01) face the same SP, Hudson, and both are dealing with significant order-position penalties. While we rely on wind-out factors to keep them viable, they are near the bottom of our efficiency range and are the first candidates to be pinch-hit or replaced if the early frames show stagnation. With **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is tested; we are keeping a close eye on the bench status of **Seiya Suzuki** and prospect-level assets like **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Henry Bolte**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana** should any late-inning injury or weather-related lineup shifts occur.",
